PTSan: do not take a pointer's ID from a literal GEP base

For `begin[(end - begin) - 1]`, the optimizer leaves

  %e = ptrtoint ptr %end to i64
  %p = getelementptr i8, ptr inttoptr (i64 -1 to ptr), i64 %e

so the tagged pointer is the GEP's index and its base is the literal -1.
PTSan 0.4.0 peels a GEP to its pointer operand unconditionally, reads the
object ID out of the literal (0xffff), and checks the access against the
fallback ID's bounds with a pointer that carries the real ID. The check fails
on a valid access:

  struct V { unsigned char *begin, *end; };
  void flip(V &v) { v.begin[(v.end - v.begin) - 1] ^= 1; }

  Found bad COMPOUND access: #0. Function ID: ..., Ptr ID: 0xffff

Stop peeling at a literal base. The GEP is then its own base, its ID is read
from its value, and no strip is moved onto the literal.

This covers 16-bit IDs only. With 32-bit IDs the same change crashes the strip
hoisting (PTSanMinCutRewriter::rewrite) while building libc++, so that mode is
left as it was and still reports the access above.

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/PTSan/PTSanUtils.cpp b/llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/PTSan/PTSanUtils.cpp
index e4e8010d6..87f0d5bca 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/PTSan/PTSanUtils.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/PTSan/PTSanUtils.cpp
@@ -277,6 +277,16 @@ Use *getPTSanRewriteablePointerUse(Instruction &I) {
   }
 
   if (auto *GEP = dyn_cast<GetElementPtrInst>(&I)) {
+    // The optimizer can canonicalize pointer arithmetic done on integers so
+    // that a literal address is the GEP base and the tagged pointer is an
+    // index, as in `getelementptr i8, ptr inttoptr (i64 -1 to ptr), i64 %end`
+    // for `begin[(end - begin) - 1]`. The result then takes its ID from the
+    // index: the literal is neither its base nor a place to move a strip to.
+    // ID16 only. An ID32 strip needs the ID of its operand's base, and the
+    // strip hoisting does not expect a GEP to be one.
+    if (!Cl32BitIDs && isUntaggedConstantPtr(GEP->getPointerOperand())) {
+      return nullptr;
+    }
     return &GEP->getOperandUse(0);
   }
 
@@ -310,6 +320,10 @@ Value *getPTSanPointerPeel(Value *V) {
   }
 
   if (auto *GEP = dyn_cast<GEPOperator>(V)) {
+    // As in getPTSanRewriteablePointerUse: a literal address is not a base.
+    if (!Cl32BitIDs && isUntaggedConstantPtr(GEP->getPointerOperand())) {
+      return nullptr;
+    }
     return GEP->getPointerOperand();
   }
 
